rganizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n Godot version\n4.5\n\n\n\n\n\n### System information\n\nAndroid - Android 15 - Vulkan/Mobile\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen an Android plugin emits a signal using `GodotPlugin.emitSignal()` and passes a `java.util.HashMap` (or `java.util.Map`) as a parameter, the game crashes immediately.\nThe JNI layer attempts to call a method named `get_keys()` on the Java object, which is a method specific to Godot's internal `GodotDictionary` class, not Java's standard `HashMap`.\n**Error Log:**\n```text\nPending exception java.lang.NoSuchMethodError: no non-static method \"Ljava/util/HashMap;.get_keys()[Ljava/lang/String;\"\nJNI DETECTED ERROR IN APPLICATION: JNI CallObjectMethodV called with pending exception java.lang.NoSuchMethodError\n\n **source code:**\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/4.5/platform/android/jni_utils.cpp#L448\n```\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate an Android plugin extending GodotPlugin.\n\nEmit a signal with a HashMap as an argument:\njava\nMap<String, Object> map = new HashMap<>();\nmap.put(\"key\", \"value\");\nemitSignal(\"my_signal\", map); // Crash occurs here\n\nThe application crashes with a SIGABRT.\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A (Simple code snippet provided above is sufficient).","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://a